(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-mystery-12","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"seventh-wharf","cn":["两个月后，调查说明的[[publication|公布]]让母亲终于肯来临河。港务部门撤回失实责任表述，港史馆开始[[correct|更正]]展板。父亲的[[reputation|名誉]]无法靠一块新牌子全补回，至少不再被写成没留下警告的醉汉。负责人在开放前[[acknowledge|承认]]旧展陈错误，列明修改依据。母亲读到父亲名字，拿出眼镜又读了一遍。老陈裹着尚未恢复的伤臂，在旁边抱怨台阶还缺防滑漆，我却看见他悄悄擦了眼角。","如何[[compensate|补偿]]家属，另有手续在办理，不由秦衡那次开价决定。赵启完成所需询问后，经母亲同意来见她，递上亲笔[[apology|道歉]]。她没有替他免去责任，只说以后别人再问，请说真话。我不再只想着[[revenge|报复]]，那带不回船上的乘客。真正出现的[[peace|平静]]很小：路上有人问父亲的事，母亲不用先低头解释，能把那份说明摊开，让他们自己看。","旧报警钟仍由有关部门保管，待调查需要结束再决定如何[[preserve|保存]]。河灯节的[[tradition|传统]]没有因音箱骗局消失，沿岸的[[community|社群]]仍给纸灯写上亲人名字，只是不再拿怪脚印吓孩子。旧港[[renovation|改造]]留下七号浮台的位置说明与水位图。老陈要求画出栏外危险水线，不能只画漂亮的钟；施工答复终于采用他看得懂的话。他读完，把纸折好放进了工装口袋。","何警官没给我们神探的[[reward|奖励]]，送来的倒是录音副本归还收条。我开始[[cherish|珍惜]]普通东西：没改过的照片、完整纸页、父亲铁杯的响声。它们守住的[[dignity|尊严]]，是一个人说过的话不能随意被改。我们在修船铺吃了顿像[[reunion|团聚]]的晚饭，母亲也坐在桌边。老陈用没受伤的手夹走我碗里最后一块肉，程雾问要不要把杯响做铃声。他嘴里满着，急得说不出话，母亲终于笑了。","次日[[dawn|黎明]]，母亲说，既然来了，就去看海。旧票留在防水袋里，我们另买票搭正常营运的客渡船。灰色[[horizon|地平线]]渐渐亮起，这是平常的[[voyage|航程]]，有人吃早餐，老陈护着伤臂坐在背风处。到对岸，我先扶母亲跨过船边，让她走[[ashore|上岸]]。她踏稳后回头叫我，我跟着下船，想起父亲从前扶我那样。她说，到了。程雾在后面关上录音机。我们看完海，当晚陪母亲返家；这一次，潮声只是潮声，不必再替谁藏一句话。"],"en":["Two months later, [[publication|publication]] of the investigation's explanation finally brought Mum back to Linhe. The port withdrew its inaccurate allocation of blame, and the museum began to [[correct|correct]] its display. One board could not fully restore Dad's [[reputation|reputation]], but it no longer called him a drunk who left no warning. Before reopening, the manager [[acknowledge|acknowledged]] the old display's errors and listed the reasons for revision. Mum read Dad's name, then put on her glasses and read it again. Beside her, Chen complained about the steps' missing anti-slip paint, his injured arm still wrapped. I saw him quietly wipe his eye.","Arrangements to [[compensate|compensate]] families were being handled separately, not decided by Qin's offer. After the required interviews, Zhao met Mum with her consent and gave her a handwritten [[apology|apology]]. She did not remove his responsibility. She asked him to speak truthfully whenever someone next asked. I no longer thought only of [[revenge|revenge]]; it would not bring the passengers back. The new [[peace|peace]] was small: if someone asked about Dad in the street, Mum could open the explanation for them to read, instead of lowering her head to defend him first.","The old warning bell remained in official custody; plans to [[preserve|preserve]] it would wait until investigative needs ended. The lantern [[tradition|tradition]] survived the speaker trick. The riverside [[community|community]] still wrote relatives' names on paper lights, but stopped frightening children with strange footprints. Port [[renovation|renovation]] retained the platform's location and a water-level diagram. Chen demanded that it show the dangerous water marks beyond the rail, not just a handsome bell. At last the construction reply used language he understood. He read it, folded it, and put it in his work jacket.","Officer He gave us no detective's [[reward|reward]], only a receipt returning our recording copy. I began to [[cherish|cherish]] ordinary things: unaltered photographs, complete pages, the sound of Dad's cup. The [[dignity|dignity]] they protected was a person's right not to have his words changed at will. We shared a [[reunion|reunion]]-like supper in the workshop, with Mum at the table. Using his uninjured hand, Chen stole the last piece of meat from my bowl. Cheng asked whether he wanted the cup clink as a ringtone. With his mouth full, he struggled to reply. Mum finally laughed.","At [[dawn|dawn]] the next day, Mum said we should see the sea while we were here. The old ticket stayed in its waterproof bag; we bought new tickets for a regularly operating passenger ferry. The grey [[horizon|horizon]] brightened. It was an ordinary [[voyage|voyage]]: passengers ate breakfast, and Chen sheltered his injured arm in a seat out of the wind. At the other side, I helped Mum over the boat's edge so she could go [[ashore|ashore]] first. Once steady, she turned and called my name. I followed, remembering how Dad had once helped me. 'We're here,' she said. Cheng switched off her recorder behind us. After seeing the sea, we accompanied Mum home that evening. This time the tide was only the tide, with no hidden words to find."]});
